    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d831">

                <pb facs="0769" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.6311/281</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-20T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 2.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2031. Your 2166, April 16, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d831-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    has just verbally given me assurances that safe-conduct will be accorded to the
                    steamer on which Austro-Hungarian diplomats and consuls and German consuls from
                    China embark.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
